(2, 31, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I', 'The nurse is caring for a patient who recently started continuous renal replacement therapy (CRRT). A sudden drop in blood pressure and disconnection of the tubing is reported. The nurse''s priority is to:', '["Change the CRRT filter", "Contact the physician immediately", "Flush the tubing with saline and continue", "Clamp the lines and prepare for volume resuscitation"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Clamp the lines and prepare for volume resuscitation.', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I'),
(2, 32, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I', 'The client with an external arteriovenous shunt in place for haemodialysis is at risk for bleeding. The priority nurse action would be to:', '["Ensure that small clamps are attached to the arteriovenous shunt dressing", "Check the results of the prothrombin time as they are determined", "serve the site once as time permits during the shift", "Check the shunt for the presence of bruit and thrill"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Ensure that small clamps are attached to the arteriovenous shunt dressing.', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I'),
(2, 33, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I', 'Which of the following interventions is critical for preventing infection in a patient with a peritoneal dialysis catheter?', '["Regular flushing of the catheter with saline", "Limiting fluid intake", "Maintaining strict aseptic technique during catheter care", "Using alcohol wipes only after dialysis"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Maintaining strict aseptic technique during catheter care.', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I'),
(2, 34, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I', 'During hemodialysis, diffusion is the primary method for:', '["Removing fluid from the blood", "Removing excess fluid from the blood by pressure", "Removing waste products and excess solutes", "Transporting proteins"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Removing waste products and excess solutes.', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I'),
(2, 35, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I', 'Which of the following best describes the main function of dialysate in dialysis?', '["Controls patient''s heartbeat", "Absorbs blood", "Removes toxins and excess substances", "Supplies nutrients"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Removes toxins and excess substances.', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I'),
(2, 36, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I', 'The primary purpose of dialysis is to:', '["Increase urine production", "Replace kidney function for waste removal", "Produce red blood cells", "Stabilize blood pressure permanently"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Dialysis removes waste products and excess fluid when kidneys cannot.', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I'),
(2, 37, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I', 'which of the following is not a vascular access for haemodialysis', '["Peritoneal membrane", "AV Fistula", "AV Graft", "Temporary Catheter"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Peritoneal membrane.', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I'),
(2, 38, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I', 'A high conductivity alarm on the dialysis machine most likely means:', '["Concentrate is over-proportioned relative to water", "Arterial pressure is low", "Air is in the venous line and blood return", "Air is in the venous line"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Concentrate is over-proportioned relative to water.', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I'),
(2, 39, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I', 'The urea reduction ratio (URR) is calculated as:', '["(Pre-dialysis urea − post-dialysis urea) ÷ pre-dialysis urea × 100", "(Post-dialysis urea − pre-dialysis urea) × dialysis time", "Post-dialysis urea ÷ pre-dialysis urea", "Pre-dialysis urea × time on dialysis"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A URR of 65% or more shows adequate dialysis.', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I'),
(2, 40, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I', 'A low conductivity alarm during haemodialysis most likely means:', '["The dialysate is too dilute (concentrate problem)", "The patient is hypertensive", "The blood line is kinked near the patient", "The blood line is kinked"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Stop dialysis flow to the dialyser; hypotonic dialysate causes haemolysis.', 'NNP 415 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing I'),
(2, 41, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I', 'Which type of kidney disease is often associated with "foamy" urine due to proteinuria?', '["Acute kidney injury", "Renal artery stenosis", "Nephrotic syndrome", "Polycystic kidney disease"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Nephrotic syndrome.', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I'),
(2, 42, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I', 'A patient with stage 4 chronic kidney disease asks what type of diet they should follow. You explain the patient should follow a:', '["Low protein, high sodium, high potassium, high phosphate diet", "Low protein, low sodium, low potassium, low phosphate diet", "High protein, low sodium, low potassium, high phosphate diet", "Low protein, low sodium, low potassium, high phosphate diet"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Low protein, low sodium, low potassium, low phosphate diet.', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I'),
(2, 43, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I', 'A GFR consistently below 15 mL/min/1.73m² is categorized as:', '["CKD Stage 4", "CKD Stage 3", "CKD Stage 5", "AKI"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: CKD Stage 5.', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I'),
