(2, 52, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I', 'Which stage of CKD is characterized by a glomerular filtration rate (GFR) below 15 mL/min/1.73m²?', '["Stage 5", "Stage 4", "Stage 1", "Stage 3"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Stage 5 CKD, or end-stage renal disease, is defined by a GFR below 15.', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I'),
(2, 53, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I', 'Glomerulonephritis is characterized by which of the following?', '["Enlargement of the renal tubules", "Inflammation of the renal pelvis", "Reduction in blood flow to the kidneys", "Inflammation of the glomeruli"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Glomerulonephritis is an inflammatory condition affecting the kidney’s glomeruli.', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I'),
(2, 54, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I', 'A 24-hour urine protein test indicating proteinuria >3.5 g/day is a diagnostic criterion for:', '["Nephrotic syndrome", "Acute tubular necrosis", "Hypertensive nephrosclerosis", "Urinary tract infection"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Nephrotic syndrome.', 'NNP 417 · Medical-Surgical Nephrology I'),
