(2, 96, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 416 · Nutrition and Dietetics in Nephrology Nursing', 'Foods high in potassium that should be limited for CKD patients include:', '["Bananas and oranges", "Apples and grapes", "Bread and eggs", "Rice and pasta"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Bananas and oranges.', 'NNP 416 · Nutrition and Dietetics in Nephrology Nursing'),
(2, 97, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 416 · Nutrition and Dietetics in Nephrology Nursing', 'The Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension (DASH) diet, which is often recommended for CKD patients, emphasizes:', '["High levels of saturated fats", "High protein intake", "Low sodium and high potassium foods", "Low carbohydrate intake"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Low sodium and high potassium foods.', 'NNP 416 · Nutrition and Dietetics in Nephrology Nursing'),
(2, 98, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 416 · Nutrition and Dietetics in Nephrology Nursing', 'Which food is highest in potassium?', '["White rice, boiled", "White rice", "Baked potato with skin", "Cabbage"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Baked potato with skin.', 'NNP 416 · Nutrition and Dietetics in Nephrology Nursing'),
(2, 99, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 416 · Nutrition and Dietetics in Nephrology Nursing', 'The patient is concerned about taking phosphate binders with meals. The nurse explains that this is necessary to:', '["Bind dietary phosphorus before absorption", "Enhance protein absorption", "Improve digestion of dietary fat", "Prevent constipation"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Bind dietary phosphorus before absorption.', 'NNP 416 · Nutrition and Dietetics in Nephrology Nursing'),
(2, 100, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Afternoon (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 416 · Nutrition and Dietetics in Nephrology Nursing', 'When educating a patient with CKD about dietary restrictions, the nurse knows to emphasize limiting foods high in:', '["Fiber", "Potassium and phosphorus", "Protein only", "Simple carbohydrates"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Potassium and phosphorus.', 'NNP 416 · Nutrition and Dietetics in Nephrology Nursing'),
(3, 1, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'Convergence model of communications another name for ?', '["Spiral model", "Transmission model", "Agenda setting model", "Interactive model"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Interactive model.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 2, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'The followings are some coping strategies frequently adopted by caregivers except', '["Re -enforcement of Social support", "Confrontation", "Self-control", "Depression"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Depression.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 3, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'Interferences that affect the accuracy of the communication exchange is term', '["Barrier", "Noise", "Context", "Feed back"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Barrier.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 4, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'A family caregiver reports emotional exhaustion, irritability, poor sleep and loss of interest in caregiving activities. Which condition is most likely?', '["Acute psychosis", "Burnout", "Euphoria", "Normal adaptation"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Burnout.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 5, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'Liner model (transmission model) of communication was founded by ???', '["Osgood and Schramm 1950", "Dr. Maxwell McCombs and Dr. Donald Lewis Shaw", "Frank Dance In 1967", "Shannon and Weaver in 1949"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Shannon and Weaver in 1949.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 6, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'A newly diagnosed CKD patient says, "My life is finished because I will never be healthy again." Which nursing response is most therapeutic?', '["\"Many people have CKD, so there is nothing to worry about.\"", "\"You should not think negatively.\"", "\"Tell me more about what having CKD means to you.\"", "\"You will eventually get used to dialysis.\""]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: "Tell me more about what having CKD means to you.".', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 7, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'Which communication technique is most appropriate when discussing sensitive issues with a renal patient?', '["Active listening", "Changing the subject", "Frequent interruption", "Giving false reassurance"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Active listening.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 8, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'Which of the following psychiatric disorders is most common in patients with end-stage renal disease?', '["Anxiety", "Obsessive compulsive disorder", "Bipolar disorder", "Depression"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Depression.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 9, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'A patient says, "If I follow the diet strictly, I''ll get a transplant." This is which stage of grief?', '["Denial", "Anger", "Bargaining", "Acceptance"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Bargaining.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 10, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'A patient from a cultural background that does not value blood transfusions requires a procedure that might involve transfusion. The nurse should first:', '["Pressure the patient to accept the transfusion", "Inform the patient of the medical necessity for the procedure", "Document the refusal and proceed with standard treatment", "Discuss alternatives and respect the patient''s beliefs"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Discuss alternatives and respect the patient''s beliefs.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 11, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'Which of the following factor does not affect illness perception?', '["Background", "Race", "Wealth", "Faith"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Wealth.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 12, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'A patient avoids telling friends about being on dialysis because of fear of discrimination. What is this an example of?', '["Stigmatization", "Socialization", "Social integration", "Rehabilitation"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Stigmatization.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 13, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'At the bottom level of communication pyramid is?????', '["Transpersonal communication", "Spiritual communication", "Intrapersonal communication", "Interpersonal communication"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Intrapersonal communication.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 14, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'Which strategy is beneficial in preventing depression among patients with CKD?', '["Discontinuing social interactions", "Avoiding discussions about their disease", "Encouraging physical activity within their capacity", "Isolation from support groups"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Physical activity can improve mood and quality of life, helping to prevent', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 15, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'Which of the following is not among the six stages of psychological adaptation to illness?', '["Exhaustion", "Denial", "Denial and shock", "Anger"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Exhaustion.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 16, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'When caring for a patient from a different cultural background, which action demonstrates cultural competence?', '["Actively seeking to understand the patient''s cultural practices and beliefs", "Avoiding discussions about the patient''s beliefs", "Only using written materials in English to explain care to the patient and family", "Only using written educational materials"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Actively seeking to understand the patient''s cultural practices and beliefs.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 17, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'A patient undergoing long-term haemodialysis reports persistent sadness, loss of interest and social withdrawal. Which condition should the nurse suspect?', '["Depression", "Phobia", "Delirium", "Mania"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Depression.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 18, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'A patient with chronic kidney disease refuses a kidney transplant, stating concerns about surgery and potential complications. The nurse''s best response is:', '["\"You need to reconsider, as this is your only option.\"", "\"It''s important to understand your concerns; let''s discuss them together.\"", "\"We cannot help you if you do not follow medical advice.\"", "\"You will not receive further treatment if you refuse surgery.\""]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: "It''s important to understand your concerns; let''s discuss them together.".', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 19, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'This model posits that ''communication isn''t something we do to others, rather, it is an activity we do with them''', '["Transmission model", "Spiral model", "Interactive model", "Transactional model"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Transactional model.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 20, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', '.... are actions that people can take to master, tolerate, reduce or minimize the effects of stressors', '["Manage", "Defence mechanisms", "Stress", "Coping strategies"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Coping strategies.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 21, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'A patient newly diagnosed with CKD avoids social gatherings because of embarrassment about having a fistula. What intervention would best promote socialization?', '["Encourage complete withdrawal until treatment is completed", "Encourage participation in appropriate social activities and support groups", "Tell the patient to hide the fistula from everyone", "Advise the patient to avoid discussing the disease"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Encourage participation in appropriate social activities and support groups.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 22, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'Which socio-economic factor can most directly interfere with a patient''s ability to maintain regular dialysis?', '["The patient''s blood group", "Eye colour", "Blood group", "Transportation and treatment costs"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Transportation and treatment costs.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 23, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'A patient repeatedly refuses dialysis despite understanding its benefits. Which factor should the nurse assess first?', '["The patient''s educational qualifications only", "The patient''s educational qualification only", "The patient''s beliefs, fears and understanding of dialysis", "The patient''s marital status only"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: The patient''s beliefs, fears and understanding of dialysis.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 24, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'Which strategy may help alleviate anxiety in patients starting dialysis?', '["Avoiding discussion of side effects", "Reducing fluid intake", "Using medical jargon", "Providing thorough explanations of the procedure"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Educating patients about dialysis helps them feel prepared and reduces anxiety.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 25, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology', 'A CKD patient reports using herbal preparations together with prescribed medications without informing the healthcare team. What is the nurse''s best response?', '["Immediately condemn the patient''s cultural beliefs", "Assess the herbal therapy and educate the patient about possible risks and interactions", "Tell the patient that all traditional medicine is ineffective", "Tell the patient all traditional remedies are always harmless"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Assess the herbal therapy and educate the patient about possible risks and interactions.', 'GST 401 · Applied Psychology & Sociology'),
(3, 26, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'Which memory loses its contents when power is switched off?', '["Compact disc", "ROM", "Hard disk", "RAM"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: RAM.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 27, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'Which one of the following is an example of the browser software?', '["Notepad", "Internet explorer", "Internet navigator", "Microsoft Word"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Internet explorer.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 28, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'What is the meaning of rebooting in the system?', '["To turn off", "To scan", "Installing a program", "Restarting Computer"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Restarting Computer.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 29, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'Which computer processes continuous data such as temperature or pressure?', '["Analog", "Mainframe", "Digital", "Palmtop"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Analog.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 30, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'Delivering clinical care remotely using ICT is called:', '["Data transmission", "E-mail", "Networking", "Telemedicine"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Telemedicine.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 31, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'Which of the following is an input device?', '["VDU (visual display unit)", "Mouse", "Printer", "Plotter"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Mouse.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 32, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'Which is a diagnostic device in ICT for health care?', '["Ultrasound scan", "Cardiac monitor", "Physiotherapy unit", "Pulse oximeter"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Ultrasound scan.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 33, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'Which statement about "h.s." is CORRECT?', '["It means \"heart sounds\" only", "It means \"hora somni\"", "It means \"high saline\"", "It means \"hourly specimen\""]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: It means "hora somni".', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 34, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'An order reads "paracetamol 1 g PRN." PRN stands for:', '["Pro re nata", "Prior to renal nutrition", "Per rectum nightly", "Post-renal nursing"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Pro re nata.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 35, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'Processing data in groups at scheduled times is called:', '["On-line processing", "Batch processing", "Real-time processing", "Multi-user processing"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Batch processing.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 36, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', '"NPO after midnight" is written on a pre-operative chart. NPO means:', '["Nothing prescribed overnight", "Nil per os", "Normal per oral intake", "Non-parenteral only"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Nil per os.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 37, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'The central processing unit is located in the _____', '["Monitor", "Memory unit", "Hard disk", "System unit"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: System unit.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 38, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'A computer is accurate, but if the result of a computation is false, what is the main reason for it?', '["Distraction", "Power failure", "Incorrect data entry", "The computer circuits"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Incorrect data entry.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 39, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'In a renal unit, ESRD and AKI are both used in documentation. Which pairing is correct?', '["ESRD = End-Stage Renal Dialysis; AKI = Advanced Kidney Impairment", "ESRD = Established Renal Disease; AKI = Acute Kidney Infection", "ESRD = End-Stage Renal Disease; AKI = Acute Kidney Injury", "ESRD = Early Stage Renal Disease; AKI = Acute Kidney Insufficiency"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: ESRD = End-Stage Renal Disease; AKI = Acute Kidney Injury.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 40, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology', 'What is smallest unit of an information/data storage?', '["A bit", "A byte", "A block", "A nibble"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: A bit.', 'GST 402 · Information Communication Technology'),
(3, 41, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'A dialysis nurse fails to monitor a patient''s access site as per protocol, and the patient suffers a haemorrhage. The hospital is held liable for the nurse''s act. This legal principle is:', '["Volenti non fit injuria", "Contributory negligence", "Res ipsa loquitur", "Vicarious liability"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Res ipsa loquitur.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 42, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'The core legal/professional principle behind nursing documentation is best summarised as:', '["''If it wasn''t documented, it wasn''t done''", "Documentation is optional if care was given correctly", "Only negative events need to be documented", "Documentation can be completed weeks later without issue"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Accurate, timely documentation is a nurse''s primary legal protection — undocumented care is very difficult to prove was ever given.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 43, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', '''Veracity'' as an ethical principle in nursing means:', '["Fairness in resource distribution", "Truthfulness and honesty with patients", "Avoiding harm", "Loyalty and faithfulness to commitments"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Veracity is the ethical duty to be truthful and honest with patients about their condition and care.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 44, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'A nurse is caring for a patient who is refusing treatment for his condition. The patient''s family is pressuring the nurse to persuade the patient to accept treatment. What should the nurse do?', '["Respect the patient''s autonomy and allow him refuse treatment.", "Consult with another nurse to determine the best course of action", "Persuade the patient to accept treatment to satisfy the family''s wishes", "Seek a court order to force the patient to accept treatment"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Respecting patient autonomy means allowing a competent patient to refuse treatment, even under family pressure.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 45, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'A nephrology nurse is developing an educational program on organ donation. Which ethical principle should be emphasized to participants?', '["Beneficence", "Autonomy", "Justice", "Non-maleficence"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Beneficence.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 46, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'What is informed consent in nursing?', '["The process of providing information to a patient about the risks and benefits of a specific procedure or treatment", "The process of respecting patients right to refuse or withdraw from a specific procedure or treatment", "The process of ensuring that a patient understands and agrees to a specific procedure or treatment", "The process of obtaining permission from a patient to perform a specific procedure or treatment"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Informed consent centres on the patient genuinely understanding and agreeing to a procedure.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 47, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', '''Non-maleficence'' as an ethical principle means:', '["Doing no harm to the patient", "Being honest with the patient", "Being fair and just to all patients", "Doing good for the patient"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Non-maleficence is the principle of ''first, do no harm'' — avoiding actions that could injure the patient.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 48, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'A failure in professional duty, practice or skill that leads to injury or harm to the patient is termed as-', '["Misunderstanding", "Negligence", "Crime", "Malpractice"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A professional failure causing patient harm is malpractice.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 49, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'The Belmont Report''s 3 core ethical principles are:', '["Autonomy, Beneficence, Justice", "Consent, Privacy, Fairness", "Honesty, Accuracy, Transparency", "Safety, Dignity, Respect"]'::jsonb, 0, 'These three principles form the foundational framework most modern research ethics guidelines build upon.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 50, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'What is the most common source of malpractice for Nurses?', '["Medication errors", "Negligent delegation", "HIPPA complaints", "Privacy violation"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Medication errors.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 51, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'A patient with advanced cancer requests discontinuation of chemotherapy. The nurse supports this decision based on:', '["Justice", "Beneficence", "Autonomy", "Nonmaleficence"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Autonomy respects the patient''s right to self-determination.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 52, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'A critically-ill patient has a "Living Will" in the chart. The patient\''s condition has deteriorated, but the spouse wants \"everything done\" regardless of the patient\''s wishes. Which ethical principle is the spouse violating?', '["Justice", "Autonomy", "Beneficence", "Non-maleficence"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Overriding a patient''s documented wishes (Living Will) disregards their autonomy.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 53, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'The ''Beneficence'' principle obligates the nurse to:', '["Simply avoid causing harm", "Always follow the patient''s exact instructions regardless of clinical judgement", "Distribute resources equally", "Actively act in ways that promote the patient''s wellbeing and best interests"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Beneficence goes beyond avoiding harm (non-maleficence) — it obligates the nurse to actively act for the patient''s good and wellbeing.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 54, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'The physician instructed the Nurse in the ICU to run a slow code as the family was not agreed for DNR. The approach used here to help the patient and family in the end of life is termed as:', '["DNR", "Life Support", "Ethical Dilemma", "Spiritual support"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Performing a deliberately less-aggressive code due to family/DNR disagreement is a classic ethical dilemma in critical care.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 55, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'Which is NOT an element of negligence?', '["Intent to harm", "Breach of duty", "Duty of care", "Resulting damage"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Intent to harm.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 56, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'In a case where a patient requires dialysis but refuses due to cultural beliefs, the nurse should:', '["Ignore the cultural beliefs and enforce treatment", "Respect the patient''s autonomy and document the refusal", "Inform the family about the refusal", "Persuade the patient to accept treatment based on health risks"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Respect the patient''s autonomy and document the refusal.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 57, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'Which of the following BEST distinguishes malpractice from simple negligence?', '["Malpractice only applies to doctors", "Malpractice only applies to doctors, while negligence applies to nurses and others", "Malpractice never results in injury", "Malpractice is professional negligence arising from failure to meet the standard expected of a professional"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Malpractice is professional negligence arising from failure to meet the standard expected of a professional.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 58, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'Nursing ethics is defined by', '["Moral principles and values", "Written rules", "Standard of care", "Policy and procedures"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Moral principles and values.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 59, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'The Helsinki Declaration establishes that:', '["Consent is optional if the research benefits many people", "Subject wellbeing takes precedence over the interests of science/society", "Science''s interests always come first", "Only adult subjects may ever be studied"]'::jsonb, 1, 'This declaration puts the individual research subject''s welfare above any broader scientific or societal gain.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 60, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'The right to withdraw from a research study at any time is part of the subject''s right to:', '["Data ownership", "Self-determination", "Anonymity only", "Compensation"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Being free to change one''s mind and leave a study without penalty is a core aspect of a subject''s autonomy over their own participation.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 61, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'Laws refer to statutes or written rules of conduct, while ethics refers to:', '["Norms of the society within which patient lives", "Written rules of conduct that are enforced by the courts and the nursing council", "Right and wrong or what nurses ought to do", "Right and wrong or what nurses ought to do considering patient values"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Right and wrong or what nurses ought to do considering patient values.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 62, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'An example of negligence is?', '["Touching a patient without consent", "Speaking badly of a patient in the cafeteria", "Leaving an unstable patient unattended to in the bathroom", "Yelling at a patient"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Leaving an unstable patient unattended to in the bathroom.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 63, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'Which four elements must all be proven for a nurse to be found legally negligent?', '["Consent, capacity, communication, and confidentiality", "Only that harm occurred, regardless of cause", "Duty of care, breach of duty, harm, and breach causing the harm", "Intent, motive, opportunity, and consequence"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Negligence requires proof of all four elements: a duty of care existed, that duty was breached, harm resulted, and the breach directly caused the harm.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 64, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'In nursing ethics, the principle of Justice specifically requires:', '["Treating all patients equally regardless of background", "Giving preferential treatment to paying patients", "Prioritising patients by social status", "Ignoring resource limitations entirely"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Justice in nursing means a patient''s background should never influence the quality of care they receive.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 65, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'Breach of patient confidentiality without lawful justification may expose a nurse to which type of legal action?', '["Civil liability for breach of confidentiality/privacy", "Automatic loss of citizenship", "Only a verbal warning with no formal process", "No consequence, since nurses have full immunity"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Unjustified disclosure of confidential patient information can expose a nurse to civil liability for breach of confidentiality.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 66, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'A nurse investigator obtains voluntary agreement from participants after explaining risks and benefits. This ethical principle is:', '["Fidelity", "Distributive justice", "Informed consent", "Beneficence"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Informed consent.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 67, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'The Nuremberg Code primarily established the requirement for:', '["Statistical significance testing", "Voluntary consent and subject welfare", "Government funding approval", "Peer review of all studies"]'::jsonb, 1, 'This code emerged after WWII specifically to ensure research subjects freely agree to participate and that their welfare is protected.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 68, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'A nurse is asked by a patient''s employer for information about the patient''s diagnosis and prognosis. The nurse''s appropriate response is to:', '["Share only positive information", "Provide the requested information immediately, since the employer is asking on the patient''s behalf", "Share information only if the employer insists strongly", "Decline to share any information without the patient''s explicit, documented consent, citing confidentiality obligations"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Patient confidentiality obligations mean health information cannot be disclosed to third parties, including employers, without the patient''s explicit informed consent.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 69, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'In nephrology nursing, ethical considerations include all the following except:', '["Patient autonomy", "Informed consent", "Deception for patient comfort", "Respect for patient autonomy"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Deception is unethical, even if the intent is to comfort the patient.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 70, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology', 'Which of the following is not an intentional tort?', '["Defamation", "False imprisonment", "Taking a patient''s pain medication", "False imprisonment of a patient"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Taking a patient''s pain medication.', 'NNP 414 · Ethico-Legal Issues in Nephrology'),
(3, 71, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics', 'A study examining the relationship between workload and burnout among dialysis nurses without manipulating variables is:', '["Experimental", "Historical", "Correlational", "Phenomenological"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Correlational.', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics'),
(3, 72, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics', 'A face-to-face data collection method is:', '["Survey", "Interview", "Observation", "Record review"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Interview.', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics'),
(3, 73, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics', 'The MOST objective data collection method is:', '["Interview", "Experiment", "Questionnaire", "Observation"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Observation.', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics'),
(3, 74, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics', 'Blood pressure measurement is:', '["Ordinal", "Qualitative", "Continuous", "Nominal"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Continuous.', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics'),
(3, 75, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics', 'Which research design is most suitable for rare diseases?', '["Case-control study", "Cohort study", "Cross-sectional study", "Experimental study"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Case-control study.', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics'),
(3, 76, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics', 'In a research study, the dependent variable represents:', '["A confounding factor", "The variable manipulated by the researcher", "A constant factor", "The outcome being measured"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: The outcome being measured.', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics'),
(3, 77, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 1 Night (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics', 'If a questionnaire measures what it is supposed to measure, it has:', '["Precision", "Validity", "Reliability", "Sensitivity"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Validity.', 'NNP 418 · Research Methods and Statistics'),
