(1, 11, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Morning (Nov 2026)', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II', 'In renal transplant patients, signs of graft rejection include all EXCEPT:', '["Tenderness over the transplant site", "Fever", "Increased blood urea nitrogen (BUN) and creatinine", "Increased urine output"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Graft rejection often decreases urine output as kidney function declines.', 'NNP 420 · Principles & Practice of Nephrology Nursing II'),
