(3, 36, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Which is a classic local sign of inflammation?', '["Redness", "Bradycardia", "Pallor", "Hypothermia"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Redness.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 37, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Cleaning of instruments can do the following EXCEPT', '["Remove soil that can inactivate disinfectants", "Remove soil that protects microorganisms during disinfection", "Remove potentially infectious microorganisms", "Make equipment become sterile"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Make equipment become sterile.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 38, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Decontamination of surfaces and medical equipment is in the following other', '["Cleaning - disinfection - sterilization", "Disinfection - sterilization - cleaning", "Cleaning - sterilization - disinfection", "Disinfection - cleaning - sterilization"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Cleaning - disinfection - sterilization.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 39, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'The etiquettes of respiratory hygiene include all EXCEPT', '["Always face away from others when coughing/sneezing", "Wash your hands after coughing/handling respiratory secretions", "Cover your nose and mouth when you cough or sneeze", "Use pocket handkerchief"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Use pocket handkerchief.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 40, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'The process used to render an object free from viable microorganisms, including viruses and bacterial spores, but not prions is called', '["Decontamination", "Sterilization", "Cleaning", "Disinfection"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Sterilization.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 41, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A person who harbours a pathogenic organism without showing symptoms but can transmit it to others is called a:', '["Carrier", "Fomite", "Reservoir only", "Vector"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Carrier.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 42, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Which group consists of microorganisms that lack a true nucleus?', '["Helminths", "Fungi", "Bacteria", "Protozoa"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Bacteria.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 43, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Which is considered a first-line physical defence against infection?', '["T lymphocytes", "Intact skin", "Antibodies", "Memory cells"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Intact skin.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 44, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Container used to collect domestic waste is color coded;', '["Yellow", "Brown", "Red", "Black"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Black.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 45, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A potassium of 7.2 mmol/L in a dialysis patient who missed sessions is best definitively treated with:', '["Urgent haemodialysis", "Waiting for the next routine session", "Oral potassium binder alone at home", "High potassium diet"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Stabilise the heart with calcium first.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 46, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', '????.. is intended for use for decontamination on inanimate surfaces (environment and equipment).', '["Detergent", "Disinfectant", "Water", "Antiseptic solution"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Disinfectant.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 47, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Grapefruit juice should be avoided in patients on tacrolimus or cyclosporine because it:', '["Causes kidney stones", "Causes hypoglycaemia", "Lowers drug levels and causes rejection", "Raises drug levels and toxicity"]'::jsonb, 3, 'It inhibits the CYP3A4 enzyme.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 48, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A temporary dialysis catheter is preferably placed in the:', '["Radial artery", "Femoral artery", "Subclavian vein first choice", "Right internal jugular vein"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Subclavian catheters cause stenosis that can block future fistulas.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 49, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A nurse should never take blood pressure or insert an IV in the arm with:', '["A wristwatch", "A tattoo", "A working AV fistula", "A plaster cast for a past fracture"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Protect the access arm.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 50, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Dry weight means:', '["The weight without clothes only", "The weight at which the patient has no excess fluid and is normotensive", "The weight before dialysis", "The weight measured before dialysis"]'::jsonb, 1, 'It is reassessed regularly.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 51, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A deceased donor kidney is usually kept on ice and transplanted ideally within about:', '["10 minutes", "24–36 hours (cold ischaemia time)", "5 days", "2 weeks"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Longer cold ischaemia increases delayed graft function.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 52, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Restless legs and pruritus in dialysis patients are often related to:', '["Excess exercise", "Inadequate dialysis and high phosphate", "Low urea", "High haemoglobin"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Check dialysis adequacy and phosphate control.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 53, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Kidney transplant recipients should avoid which vaccine?', '["Influenza injection", "Pneumococcal vaccine", "Live vaccines such as yellow fever and MMR", "Hepatitis B vaccine"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Live vaccines can cause disease when immunosuppressed.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 54, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A patient acquires an infection while receiving care in a healthcare facility that was not present or incubating at admission. This is best described as:', '["Healthcare-associated infection", "Community-acquired infection", "Genetic infection", "Autoimmune disease"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Healthcare-associated infection.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 55, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'The fluid allowance per day for a dialysis patient is usually:', '["Exactly 3 litres for everyone", "5 litres regardless of urine", "Urine output plus about 500 mL", "No fluid at all"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Interdialytic weight gain should be limited.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 56, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Which is the best definition of a reservoir of infection?', '["The method by which microorganisms are destroyed", "The immune response against microorganisms in the body", "The route by which microorganisms enter the body", "The place where an infectious organism normally lives and multiplies"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: The place where an infectious organism normally lives and multiplies.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 57, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'In the sepsis therapeutic concept, the first choice of drug is?', '["Gram-negative antibiotics", "Gram-positive antibiotics", "Anti-fungal", "Broad-spectrum antibiotics"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Broad-spectrum antibiotics.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 58, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A dialysis patient develops chest pain, dyspnoea and hypotension shortly after a session starts with a new dialyser. This may be:', '["Hyperkalaemia from food", "Fluid overload from the diet", "Normal dialysis", "A first-use (dialyser) reaction"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Stop dialysis, do not return the blood, and give support as ordered.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 59, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'What is the primary purpose of culture media in microbiology?', '["To provide conditions that support microbial growth", "To prevent bacterial multiplication in specimens", "To destroy microorganisms", "To prevent bacterial multiplication"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: To provide conditions that support microbial growth.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 60, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Muscle cramps during haemodialysis are usually due to:', '["Excess calcium", "Rapid fluid removal and low blood volume", "Hyperglycaemia", "Infection"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Reduce UF rate and give saline if needed.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 61, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Air embolism during haemodialysis is treated by:', '["Sitting the patient upright", "Giving IV fluids only", "Increasing the blood flow", "Clamping the lines and placing the patient on the left side, head down"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Give 100% oxygen and call for help.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 62, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A nurse is about to perform a procedure involving possible exposure to blood. Which action is appropriate?', '["Avoid hand hygiene if gloves are worn", "Wear appropriate personal protective equipment based on anticipated exposure", "Wear gloves only if the patient is known to have an infection", "Wear gloves only if the patient is known to have HIV"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Wear appropriate personal protective equipment based on anticipated exposure.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 63, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Tumour lysis syndrome can cause AKI because of high levels of:', '["Uric acid, phosphate and potassium", "Calcium and vitamin D", "Glucose and albumin", "Iron and copper"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Prevent with hydration and allopurinol or rasburicase.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 64, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Uraemic encephalopathy may present with:', '["Confusion, asterixis and seizures", "Improved memory", "Bradycardia only", "Hearing improvement"]'::jsonb, 0, 'It improves with dialysis.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 65, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Adult CPR compressions should be:', '["120-140/min at 4 cm", "80-100/min at 3 cm", "60-80/min at 2 cm", "100-120/min at 5-6 cm"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: 100-120/min at 5-6 cm.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 66, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Container used to collect infectious waste is color coded', '["Brown", "Red", "Black", "Yellow"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Yellow.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 67, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A urine specimen is required for bacterial culture. Which practice is most important to obtain a reliable result?', '["Leave the specimen uncovered for several hours", "Collect it from any available container", "Add antiseptic to the specimen", "Collect the specimen using an appropriate sterile technique"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Collect the specimen using an appropriate sterile technique.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 68, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A patient on haemodialysis is at risk of hepatitis B, so staff and patients should:', '["Share dialysis machines freely", "Be vaccinated and have antibody levels checked", "Reuse needles", "Avoid all gloves"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Follow strict infection control.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 69, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Ideal interdialytic weight gain is usually less than about:', '["No limit", "2–2.5 kg (or about 4% of dry weight)", "8 kg", "10% of body weight"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Large gains cause hypotension and cramps on dialysis.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 70, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Aminoglycoside nephrotoxicity is reduced by:', '["Combining with NSAIDs", "Giving doses more often", "Monitoring drug levels and avoiding prolonged courses", "Restricting fluids"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Check creatinine and trough levels.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 71, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A patient develops an infection after microorganisms from an infected wound are transferred to another patient through a healthcare worker''s hands. The healthcare worker''s hands represent the:', '["Mode of transmission", "Portal of exit", "Portal of entry", "Reservoir"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Mode of transmission.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 72, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A nurse sustains an accidental needle-stick injury after caring for a patient. What should the nurse do first?', '["Continue working and report it at the end of the week if there is no bleeding", "Apply a tourniquet above the injury", "Immediately wash the affected area and report the exposure according to hospital protocol", "Continue working and report it at the end of the month"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Immediately wash the affected area and report the exposure according to hospital protocol.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 73, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Which patient is at greatest risk of developing infection?', '["Patient receiving immunosuppressive therapy", "Patient without invasive procedures", "Patient with normal immune function", "Healthy adult with intact skin"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Patient receiving immunosuppressive therapy.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 74, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Catheter-related bloodstream infection in a dialysis patient presents with:', '["Low blood sugar", "Fever and rigors during or after dialysis", "Facial palsy", "Bradycardia"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Take blood cultures and start antibiotics.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 75, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'The primary purpose of diagnostic microbiology is to:', '["Increase microbial growth in patients", "Replace clinical assessment", "Identify microorganisms responsible for disease", "Prevent all normal flora"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Identify microorganisms responsible for disease.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 76, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Which method is most appropriate for sterilizing heat-stable surgical instruments?', '["Wiping with a dry cloth", "Cleaning with soap only", "Rinsing with tap water", "Autoclaving with pressurized steam"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Autoclaving with pressurized steam.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 77, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Magnesium sulfate toxicity is of particular concern in pre-eclampsia with renal impairment because:', '["Magnesium increases urine output", "Magnesium is metabolised by the liver", "Magnesium is metabolised by the liver, so renal impairment has no effect on its levels", "Magnesium is excreted by the kidneys, so reduced GFR causes accumulation"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Magnesium is excreted by the kidneys, so reduced GFR causes accumulation.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 78, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'The drug of choice for seizure prophylaxis and treatment in eclampsia is:', '["Phenytoin", "Diazepam", "Phenobarbital", "Magnesium sulfate"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Magnesium sulfate.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 79, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A woman with advanced cervical cancer develops anuria and rising creatinine. The MOST likely cause is:', '["Prerenal dehydration only, from poor oral intake and vomiting", "Diabetic nephropathy", "Prerenal dehydration only", "Bilateral ureteric obstruction from tumour extension, causing obstructive uropathy"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Bilateral ureteric obstruction from tumour extension, causing obstructive uropathy.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 80, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A nurse administering magnesium sulfate notes absent patellar reflexes and a respiratory rate of 10/min. The FIRST action is to:', '["Give furosemide", "Stop the infusion and prepare calcium gluconate", "Increase the infusion rate", "Continue and recheck in 1 hour"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Stop the infusion and prepare calcium gluconate.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 81, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Mild physiological hydronephrosis in pregnancy is most commonly seen on the:', '["Both sides equally, due to diabetes", "Left side, due to progesterone only and compression by the sigmoid colon", "Right side, due to uterine dextrorotation and progesterone-induced smooth muscle relaxation", "Neither side, as it is always pathological"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Right side, due to uterine dextrorotation and progesterone-induced smooth muscle relaxation.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 82, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'In a kidney transplant recipient planning pregnancy, which immunosuppressant must be stopped or switched beforehand because of teratogenicity?', '["Azathioprine", "Prednisolone", "Mycophenolate mofetil", "Tacrolimus"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Mycophenolate mofetil.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 83, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Which pregnancy-related condition is classically associated with acute cortical necrosis of the kidneys?', '["Placental abruption with severe haemorrhage", "Gestational diabetes", "Braxton Hicks contractions", "Mild hyperemesis"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Placental abruption with severe haemorrhage.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 84, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'In evaluating the urological system in children, one of the following is not necessary.', '["A history of abdominal pain", "An obstetric scan to determine the presence of fallopian tubes", "Assessment of the urinary stream", "A history of burning sensation while passing urine"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: An obstetric scan to determine the presence of fallopian tubes.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 85, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Diet as supportive management of childhood nephrotic syndrome entails one of the following:', '["Curtail cholesterol and saturated fatty acids", "Encourage eating of fries and canned foods", "Liberal fluid intake with severe oedema", "Strict protein restriction"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Curtail cholesterol and saturated fatty acids.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 86, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A child with acute kidney injury has markedly reduced urine output. Which finding requires the nurse''s most immediate attention?', '["Hyperkalaemia with ECG changes", "Reduced appetite", "Mild facial oedema", "Mild fatigue"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Hyperkalaemia with ECG changes.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 87, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'When taking the history of a child suspected of having renal disease, which information is particularly important?', '["Preferred school subjects", "Favourite food and recreational activities", "Previous urinary tract infections and urine characteristics", "Number of siblings only"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Previous urinary tract infections and urine characteristics.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 88, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A student nurse asks when fetal urine production begins. Which response by the nurse is most appropriate?', '["During the first trimester", "Around the end of the first trimester", "Immediately after birth", "During the second trimester"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Around the end of the first trimester.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 89, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Which instruction is most important for a child and family following kidney transplantation?', '["Take immunosuppressive medications exactly as prescribed and attend regular follow-up appointments", "Stop immunosuppressants once the child feels well", "Discontinue laboratory monitoring when creatinine becomes normal", "Stop immunosuppressants once the child feels well and the creatinine is normal"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Take immunosuppressive medications exactly as prescribed and attend regular follow-up appointments.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 90, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A core principle of palliative care (WHO) is that it:', '["Neither hastens nor postpones death", "Applies only in the last week", "Hastens death", "Excludes family"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Neither hastens nor postpones death.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 91, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'A CKD patient requires dietary modification, psychological support and social assistance. Which approach is most appropriate?', '["Interdisciplinary team management", "Nurse-only management", "Patient-only management", "Family-only management"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Interdisciplinary team management.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 92, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'The integration of artificial intelligence in nephrology nursing has the potential to:', '["Limit access to medical data for healthcare providers", "Diminish the importance of patient-centered care", "Replace the need for nursing staff and clinical judgement", "Enhance decision-making processes and predictive analytics in patient care"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Enhance decision-making processes and predictive analytics in patient care.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 93, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Sustainable development goal 3 is about', '["Achieve gender equality and empower all women and girls", "End poverty in all its forms everywhere", "Ensure healthy lives and promote wellbeing for all at all ages", "Reduce inequality within and among countries"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Ensure healthy lives and promote wellbeing for all at all ages.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 94, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Maternal mortality rate is The number of women who die as a result of childbirth and pregnancy related complications per', '["5000 live birth in a given year", "10,000 live births in a given year", "100,000 live births in a given year", "1000 live birth in a given year"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: 100,000 live births in a given year.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 95, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Actual nursing diagnosis', '["Represents a set of data that has been clinically obtained during nursing care", "Represents a state that has been clinically validated by identified defining characteristics", "Represents a state that has been validated by evidence", "Represents a set of clinically proven statements by identifiable defining labels."]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Represents a state that has been clinically validated by identified defining characteristics.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 96, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'In nephrology nursing, which of the following represents a significant shift in practice toward patient-centered care?', '["Sole reliance on healthcare provider expertise", "Increased focus on diagnostic testing only", "Enhanced involvement of patients in shared decision-making", "Limited patient access to their medical records"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is: Enhanced involvement of patients in shared decision-making.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 97, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'In a leadership role, a nephrology nurse should promote which of the following to enhance team performance?', '["Continuous education and professional development", "Individual accountability over collaboration", "Resistance to change in practice", "Strict adherence to hierarchical decision-making"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: Continuous education and professional development.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 98, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'In managing a patient with chronic kidney disease, the nephrology nurse collaborates with a dietitian. What is the primary goal of this collaboration?', '["To develop an individualized nutrition plan that meets the patient''s needs", "To ensure the patient receives the cheapest diet available", "To ensure the patient receives adequate dialysis", "To refer the patient for kidney transplant evaluation"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The correct answer is: To develop an individualized nutrition plan that meets the patient''s needs.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 99, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', 'Palliative care needs', '["Urgent referrals only", "Urgent referrals and continuous care", "Timely referrals", "Planned and urgent"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is: Urgent referrals and continuous care.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)'),
(3, 100, 'Nephrology Nursing Mock — Day 2 Night (Nov 2026)', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)', '______ refers to any health issues that concerns many countries and is affected by transnational determinants', '["Global health", "Natural disasters", "Global warming", "Global health issues"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is: Global health issues.', 'Comprehensive Nephrology Revision (Dialysis, Transplant, Emergencies & Infection Control)');
